From 87565ec44e4ae14496a2da2a1dfc96abb2f8a54c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <blue@aquarat.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 11:03:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(ml): ggml Vulkan session backend for CLIP visual
 models

Adds a GgmlSession that runs CLIP image encoders on the GPU through
libclipvit (ggml + Vulkan) while the text tower, facial recognition and OCR
stay on ONNX Runtime. It follows the ArmNN and RKNN session layout:

- sessions/ggml/loader.py: ctypes binding for libclipvit.so; the backend is
  available when the library loads and a Vulkan GPU is present
- sessions/ggml/convert.py: converts the open_clip visual ONNX Immich already
  downloads (including external data, memory-mapped) into a GGUF with f16 or
  Q8_0 weights, so the weights are exactly those of the ONNX session.
  Unsupported architectures raise UnsupportedModelError
- ModelFormat.GGUF, chosen by default for CLIP visual models when the backend
  is available; the GGUF is produced on first load next to the ONNX file and
  regenerated when the weight type setting changes. Models that cannot be
  converted fall back to ONNX like other formats
- settings: MACHINE_LEARNING_GGML, GGML_PRECISION (FP32/FP16 shader math),
  GGML_WEIGHT_TYPE (f16/q8_0), GGML_FLASH_ATTN, GGML_THREADS; the GPU index
  comes from MACHINE_LEARNING_DEVICE_ID
- pyproject: ggml extra (onnxruntime + gguf), tests for format selection and
  the session

